From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:57:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0072: a guest wait for a shader's value goes on
 behind a barrier

Astro Bot's graphics queue waits about nine times an image for a flag its compute work sets to 1. Each
time the command thread submitted, then polled every 100 us until the GPU had written it: 610 suspended
waits and 300 polls an image, the GPU and the thread taking turns. The compute work is recorded before,
on the same Vulkan queue, and the GPU runs the stream in order: behind a barrier (GuestSync), everything
recorded after the wait runs after that shader, which is all the wait asks - if the shader writes the
value. BufferCache trusts an address once four waits there ended with the value, checks each trusted
wait once the writer's work is done, and revokes the address for good on a miss (the console says so).

Astro Bot, Sky Garden, production settings: label waits 47 -> 5.3 ms an image, 610 -> 74 suspensions,
14 waits passed behind a barrier, 55 -> 35 command buffers, 8.6 -> 9.2-9.5 images/s. The thread now runs
ahead into resource tables the compute work writes: two full drains an image, 33.6 ms (was 1.5).
Five addresses revoked during loading (written later than the work recorded before the wait).
